                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90ec196f-2ec7-415d-bc48-2a4d33a850e9",
                        "source_entry_id": "ceca0295-dbec-31aa-8866-2332da312d56",
                        "source_sense_id": "82f7528b-d78f-3837-be21-93e493fa4534",
                        "source_sense_description": "uithoek, een hypothetisch en oneindig ver land",
                        "target_lang_word": "Outer Mongolia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Outer Mongolia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5cd65cc-fb00-3074-9cdf-98a70e9527d6",
                                        "entry_id": "85a36518-a7e5-33fc-9fc0-105c6393dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mongolia; a region south of Siberia, west of Manchuria and north of Inner Mongolia (with closely related native Mongolian population), well north of the Great Wall, which never became an integral part of the Chinese empire, and later achieved autonomy and full independence of China, as the republic of Mongolia"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72bcc302-ffe2-4bb9-afa0-02ed4cc0a75b",
                                                "sense_id": "b5cd65cc-fb00-3074-9cdf-98a70e9527d6",
                                                "text": "The divisions of Wái Mungkú 外蒙古 or Outer Mongolia, are four lú 路 or circuits, usually called khanates from the titles of the leading chieftain khan 汗."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8e9ba04-ee44-44a7-afe3-60da2f7b90ac",
                                                "sense_id": "b5cd65cc-fb00-3074-9cdf-98a70e9527d6",
                                                "text": "He professed to have twice defeated the Sungars in Outer Mongolia and Sinkiang, once suppressed the rebellion of Moslems in Turkestan, twice put down insurrections in the Chin-ch’uan region in western Szechwan, once pacified a rebellion in Taiwan (Formosa), subjugated Burma and Annam, and twice vanquished the Gurkhas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e52a24b-53b6-4b75-a0d4-81364954faa0",
                                                "sense_id": "b5cd65cc-fb00-3074-9cdf-98a70e9527d6",
                                                "text": "Peiping regards Moscow as the revisionist headquarters. The East European satellite states, Cuba and Outer Mongolia are petty revisionists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f7750c6-8814-4380-83ca-9bdb8afe30fb",
                                                "sense_id": "b5cd65cc-fb00-3074-9cdf-98a70e9527d6",
                                                "text": "“Yalta not only severed Outer Mongolia from China, but also brought the northeastern part of China into the Soviet sphere,” he went on. “After the founding of the People’s Republic of China, our first demands to the Soviet Union were to recover Chinese sovereignty over the Changchun Railway and Port Arthur. Only then was PRC authority in northeastern China confirmed. . . . We raised the question of Outer Mongolia, but the Soviets didn’t respond."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55f68555-3e23-36b0-8ac4-c34dc6a34ffd",
                                        "entry_id": "85a36518-a7e5-33fc-9fc0-105c6393dd32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any proverbially distant or remote place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e296bdb-6eb9-43a3-b86c-2a4b4d4103f1",
                                                "sense_id": "55f68555-3e23-36b0-8ac4-c34dc6a34ffd",
                                                "text": "Nora Ludd feels much happier when making Bayer executives’ lives miserable by visiting their homes at night. He lives in a muddy ditch in the north of England, but is currently on a yoga holiday in Outer Mongolia with his tortoise animal companion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d029627-f1d1-43ed-8d3e-be691d6e80b0",
                                                "sense_id": "55f68555-3e23-36b0-8ac4-c34dc6a34ffd",
                                                "text": "Okay, so here’s an idea, Matthew: Take some of that “free” money from “legitimate sources of government,” buy a plane ticket to Outer Mongolia—and stay there."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f74aa284-719a-4551-bb25-0956e62d9fd1",
                                                "sense_id": "55f68555-3e23-36b0-8ac4-c34dc6a34ffd",
                                                "text": "Troubleshooters were supposed to remain in control, and when she and Deke had one of their discussions, she didn’t stay cool and serene. Showing a weakness like that in front of a councilor was a good way to get assigned to Outer Mongolia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7862529a-468a-4d1b-b4d4-09ffdeed6a6d",
                        "source_entry_id": "ceca0295-dbec-31aa-8866-2332da312d56",
